{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And he made the menorah, etc.</b> You will find throughout the entire account of the work that it scrutinizes the language of the deed to match the language of the commandment, and one must know why he changed regarding the menorah — for in the commandment it says <b>מְנֹרַת זָהָב</b> (a lampstand of gold), whereas here it says <b>אֶת הַמְּנוֹרָה</b> (the menorah)." "But perhaps it is as follows: according to what they said, of blessed memory, in Bekometz Rabba (Menahot 28b) — that the menorah may also be made from other metals, since it is written ״תֵּעָשֶׂה״ (it shall be made) to include [other metals] — for this reason HaShem said <b>מְנֹרַת זָהָב</b> to say that what He permitted by the inclusive term <b>תֵּעָשֶׂה</b> applies only for the generations, but in the Tabernacle it is a stringent requirement that it be of gold. And therefore He juxtaposed <b>מְנֹרַת זָהָב</b> with no break, to say that your act of making the menorah must be only of gold. Or, along these lines: <b>מְנֹרַת זָהָב</b> and not a menorah of other metals, even though I permitted them to you — and this fine point has no relevance to be stated in the account of the deed; rather, he informed us that he fulfilled the commandment of HaShem and made it of gold. Understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:09.599790301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}